    ("p", "The findings have a common pattern. Most lie at a boundary between Ninsho and something it does not own: a web framework's proxy setting (F-02), the encoding of a client-supplied key (F-04), the continuous-integration runner (F-05), a container runtime (F-08), or the way an application stores passkey owners (B-01). F-01 is instructive in another way: an earlier fix had already aligned the PASETO deny-list lifetime with the clock tolerance, and the sibling index was missed. A suite of more than two thousand passing tests did not prevent any of these, which is why this report treats the tests as scoped evidence rather than proof of security."),
